35,2,1,talk,Ryuji,,"Transport costs are a huge variable, and whole-building lets have non-refundable deposits. This creates a significant financial risk if attendance drops.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Toshio,,"Public bookings are a nightmare. The lottery and the nine-page application are far too demanding. Also, self-catering on campus is a huge time sink.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,Minako,,"It seems the evenings are where the real bonding happens, but we've lost a lot of members who simply didn't attend past away camps.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Jonathan,,"Public beds are cheap, but the reality is grim. Some clubs had eight people to a room with strict lights-out. That's not restful.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Asuka,,"@Ryuji, I found the same. The non-refundable deposits mean the remaining members would have to cover the cost of anyone who cancels late.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Ryuji,,"@Asuka, exactly. We cannot announce a fee without knowing if it will be sufficient. We need a low-risk financial model.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Toshio,,"@Ryuji, that's why we should avoid any venue that requires an administrative marathon or forces the organizers to spend hours cooking.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,Minako,,"@Toshio, but if we stay too close or separate, we miss the chance to integrate the year-groups. We need a shared living space.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Jonathan,,"@Minako, shared space is good, but not if it's a crowded dormitory. Poor sleep will ruin the final days of training.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[""Minako""],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Asuka,,"@Minako, the attendance sheets show that away camps might be too much for some. We need a balance between bonding and accessibility.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Minako""],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Ryuji,,"It sounds like we are all worried about different types of burdens: financial, administrative, social, and physical.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Toshio,,Precisely. We need a solution that minimizes the workload for the organizers while remaining sustainable.,"{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,Minako,,"I still believe that unless we are all in one place, the club will continue to drift apart.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,Jonathan,,I just want to ensure that whatever we choose doesn't result in a group of exhausted members.,"{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Asuka,,"We need to avoid the ""hidden costs"" of both money and effort. A simple, transparent system is best.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
